<!--
  This file exists so the directory survives in git.

  `apps/video-editor/Dockerfile` line ~149 has:

      COPY --from=builder /app/apps/video-editor/public ./public

  A `COPY` of a path that does not exist is a HARD BUILD FAILURE, and this
  directory did not exist - so any uncached build of video-editor failed with:

      "/app/apps/video-editor/public": not found

  The failure was invisible for a long time purely because the build was
  cached. The running container was months old, so nobody re-ran the build
  without a cache miss and nobody saw it. This is the same failure mode as
  everything else in this app: a cached artifact hiding a broken instruction.

  An empty directory would not be committed, so .gitkeep holds the path.
-->
